  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The perimeter of an isosceles right triangle is \\(2p.\\) Its area is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\((2+\\sqrt2)p\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\((2-\\sqrt2)p\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\((3-2\\sqrt2)p^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\((1-2\\sqrt2)p^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\((3+2\\sqrt2)p^2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1953-p33.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If each leg is \\(s,\\) then \\[ s(2+\\sqrt2)=2p, \\] so \\(s=p(2-\\sqrt2).\\) Therefore the area is \\[ \\begin{gathered} \\frac{s^2}{2} =\\frac{p^2(2-\\sqrt2)^2}{2}\\\\ =(3-2\\sqrt2)p^2. \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Let each leg have length \\(s\\), so the hypotenuse is \\(s\\sqrt2\\)",
        "Solve \\(s(2+\\sqrt2)=2p\\), then use area \\(\\frac{s^2}{2}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
